# Copy to .dev.vars for local `wrangler dev` overrides (gitignored).
# Nothing here is required — wrangler.jsonc's "vars" already ship working
# defaults (POLICY_MODE=allow_all). This file exists so a future OAuth or
# metered-policy activation has a documented place to put local secrets.

# POLICY_MODE=metered
# POLICY_METERED_DAILY_LIMIT=50
# POLICY_UPGRADE_URL=https://brickandmortar.dev

# The credential brickandmortar.dev/api/mcp-feedback requires before it will
# file anything from `request_a_feature`. In production it is a Worker secret
# (`wrangler secret put MCP_FEEDBACK_TOKEN`) and must match the Vercel env var
# of the same name on the brick-and-mortar project. Unset, the tool files
# nothing and reports that it failed — it never claims a send that did not
# happen.
# MCP_FEEDBACK_TOKEN=
